3️⃣ Database Latency / Connection Exhaustion Incident



“We had a backend system using a managed relational database, and over time the workload became more read-heavy. During peak hours,
users started experiencing API timeouts.

From an impact perspective, requests were backing up and application thread pools were getting blocked.

Our monitoring showed database latency spikes, and we also saw that the database had reached its maximum connection limit.

As an immediate fix, we temporarily scaled the database and tuned the application’s connection pool to prevent runaway connections.

Longer term, we introduced read replicas and Redis caching, and moved expensive queries out of the critical request path.

The key learning was understanding the system’s hot paths and monitoring them explicitly, rather than treating the database as an infinite resource.”
